# Optional, development only (`npm run dev`). Comma-separated host names that may reach the dev server
# through a tunnel. Not used by `npm run build` / `npm start`. No secrets belong here.
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=my-name.trycloudflare.com

# Production builds read NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL from .env.production (https://milansingla.tech). Override it here for another domain (https only). Turns on canonical links, the sitemap entry,
# Open Graph URLs/image and the URLs in the structured data. If it is ever empty, none of those are emitted,
# so a wrong or temporary address can never be published. Example: https://example.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Test builds only (tests/blog-e2e.sh sets these): BLOG_CONTENT_DIR, BLOG_PUBLIC_DIR, NEXT_DIST_DIR. Never needed for a real build.
